From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:21:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: apple: enable J713 Bluetooth with scoped radio DMA

Enable the BCM4388 PCIe function and share the radio DART through explicit
ordinary SIDs for Wi-Fi and Bluetooth. Admit only inactive, rootless
managed streams with unmasked fault reporting, preserve unrelated
streams, verify RID-to-SID publication and quarantine on mapping faults.
Retain published DMA state and block unsupported takeover, reset and
suspend operations until a platform reset. Keep display support outside
this basic series.

Constrain BCM4388 allocations to one bounded high DMA aperture, publish
the context upper address through the chip's actual register and wait
for each requested firmware state using one fixed deadline. Preserve
legacy chip register layouts and DMA behavior. Add host tests for DMA
admission, publication/quarantine, address registers and state waits.

The integrated implementation has passed controller initialization,
LE discovery, repeated power cycles and concurrent Wi-Fi traffic on J713.

Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
[dylan: DART part only, as the prerequisite of 52d846f6b ("iommu/apple-dart:
 adopt J713 display streams with retained ownership"), which builds on its
 managed-SID state: apple-dart.c, the dart.h radio check, the apple,dart.yaml
 apple,managed-sids property and the sysfs ABI file with its MAINTAINERS
 entry. The Bluetooth, PCIe, J713 DTS, config and selftest parts are not
 taken; the managed-SID path stays inert without apple,managed-sids on J713.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
